// parts-db.mjs — component database + designator-pattern classifier for BOM generation.
// price1k = INR at the ~1000-module aggregate (RFQ-target basis, ±25 %); breaks are 100 pc ×1.35 and
// 5000 pc ×0.88 unless a part carries its own volume quote (`p10k`). Every entry names a second source.
// SKU-dependent parts (fuses, relays, CM chokes, magnetics, snubbers, burdens) resolve via skuOverrides.
// Ordering matters: first matching pattern wins; keep specific patterns above the catch-alls.
// `desc`, `note` and `alt` are PURCHASING TEXT — they print into the BOM pages, the line-item CSVs and
// the release schematic sheets. Write them as a specification: what the part is, its ratings, its
// acceptance rows, its second source. Never as a change log.

// The four module SKUs — every pipeline consumer iterates THIS list.
