    PS1H: { price1k: 140, p10k: 100, mpn: "ISO-GBIAS-15-2W", desc: "iso gate-bias module +15/−3 V, **2 W class**: this channel drives TWO paralleled SG2M023120LJ dies at up to f_max 203 kHz, so P_gate = n·Q_g·ΔV·f + driver I_CC2 = 1.13 W at f_r and 1.59 W at f_max — 113–159 % of a 1 W module, continuously. An overloaded module droops, the NSI66x1A VCC2 UVLO falling threshold is 9.8–11.8 V, and a sagging rail first raises R_DS(on) on the paralleled dies and then takes the channel offline at exactly the light-output-voltage corners, presenting as a control fault that is not one. The 30 kW channels drive one die (0.85 W worst) and keep the 1 W class. RFQ: C_io ≤ 5 pF for the CM budget" },
